<title>USA: Continental Air made &quot;overtures&quot; to Latam carriers.</title>
<headline>Continental Air made &quot;overtures&quot; to Latam carriers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines Inc said it made &quot;overtures&quot; to several carriers in Latin America, but declined to identify a particular target.</p>
<p>The Houston-based carrier also declined to comment on an Argentine newspaper report it was considering buying a share in Argentina's flag carrier Aerolineas Argentinas.</p>
<p>The airline, which plans to expand aggressively in South America and Asia in 1997, is currently seeking regulatory approval to serve Sao Paulo and Rio De Janiero from its Newark, N.J. hub.</p>
<p>(( New York newsdesk 212-859-1610 ))</p>
</text>
